[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/dialogue/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"n6_godric"
text = "# DRAFT
# Abbot Godric at dusk, sick in his bed since he fell in the smoke at Matins (night 6, snow). Thomas brings him something
# hot at every bell, and he sleeps and wakes and doesn't know what's happening: why there's no bell, whether it's morning.
# He doesn't know Anselm is dead: Thomas told him Anselm sleeps sound at last. Telling him what his brothers are: he
# thinks the porter is feverish, sends him to Thomas, and will tell Thomas he's coming (Suspicion +5).
== start
(The abbot lies in his bed under a heap of blankets, his beads in his fingers, his lips moving. His breath rattles.)
Godric: My son? Is it Matins? I didn't hear the bell.
Godric: Thomas says I'm not to trouble about Matins. He says the house can sing without me for one night.
-> topics

== again
(The abbot has slipped down in the bed. He opens his eyes, and takes a while to find you.)
Godric: Who is it? Oh. The porter. Is it morning?
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n6_godric_how] How are you, Father Abbot? -> how
* [if not n6_godric_anselm] Have you heard about Brother Anselm, Father Abbot? -> anselm
* [if not n6_godric_truth] Father Abbot, your brothers are not what they seem. -> truth

== how [set n6_godric_how]
Godric: Thomas says it's the smoke, in my chest. He brings me something hot at every bell, and I sleep.
Godric: I sleep so much, child. I dream I'm awake, and then I wake, and it's the same room.
-> topics

== anselm [set n6_godric_anselm]
Godric: Anselm? Thomas sat with him through Vespers. He says Anselm sleeps sound at last, poor soul, like a child.
Godric: Thirty years at our gate, and never a whole night's sleep. Let him have it.
-> topics

# He'll tell Thomas what the porter said: Suspicion +5.
== truth [set n6_godric_truth] [suspicion 5]
(He hears you out. Then he laughs, weakly, and it turns into coughing.)
Godric: My brothers? Child, you're feverish. Thomas said you might be.
Godric: Go to him. He'll give you something to help you sleep. I'll tell him you're coming.
-> topics

== leave
Godric: Pray for the house, my son. I can't seem to keep hold of the words.
"
